<section class="section wrap" id="work">
  <div class="sechead">
    <h2>Systems that ship, teams that deliver, and customers that buy</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="intro">My work sits where architecture meets the people who have to live with it. I start with questions more than answers: what do the people in this system actually need, and what keeps slowing them down? Then we build toward that together, and the engineers get better at their craft along the way.</p>
  {% set quote = "Organizations exist in as much as they provide service to humans." %}
  {% set from = "what-in-the-world-is-world-class-engineering-part-2" %}
  {% set fromTitle = "What in the World Is World-Class Engineering? Part 2" %}
  {% include "epigraph.njk" %}
  <div class="cards">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="mono teal small">n = 1</p>
      <h3>Stack Overflow</h3>
      <p class="muted">Director of Product Engineering · 2024–2026</p>
      <p>I led the Architecture Group and two full-stack teams maintaining the Public Platform, the public face of Stack Overflow, in a remote organization of about 50 developers across the US, EU and Brazil. I coordinated eight teams through a six-month re-architecture to backend-for-frontend microservices and microfrontends on Azure and GCP, and we launched on schedule. I built DORA reporting and working groups that doubled deploy frequency, cut build times by 20% and improved query response times by 5%. I also helped shape the company's AI productivity program and AI security policy, including MCP servers, AI use cases and hackathons, until every engineer was using and building AI tools.</p>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>deploy frequency</dt><dd>2×</dd></div>
        <div><dt>build times</dt><dd>−20%</dd></div>
        <div><dt>teams coordinated</dt><dd>8</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="mono teal small">n = 2</p>
      <h3>Pluralsight</h3>
      <p class="muted">Senior Director of Architecture · 2018–2024</p>
      <p>I led the architecture team for an engineering organization of up to 500 people across 65+ teams in the US, India and Australia. I connected pricing strategy to purchase integrations, and product structures to architecture and payment systems, and helped integrate the Flow and A Cloud Guru acquisitions. I led the teams that built identity, authorization, royalties and audit systems, and ran the tech radar. I oversaw the move to Kubernetes and managed Kafka, the monolith decommission, and SOX, GDPR and FedRAMP planning, and managed budgets over $5M with fellow leaders. Through all of it I worked closely with Product, Security, Data and Partnerships to put team structures and processes in place that actually served the people inside them.</p>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>teams</dt><dd>65+</dd></div>
        <div><dt>continents</dt><dd>3</dd></div>
        <div><dt>acquisitions</dt><dd>2</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="mono teal small">n = 3</p>
      <h3>Merrick Bank</h3>
      <p class="muted">AVP Systems Programming · 2008–2018</p>
      <dl class="stats">
        <div><dt>customers a month</dt><dd>4.5M</dd></div>
        <div><dt>engineers</dt><dd>2 → 16</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p>I led the teams behind web and mobile credit card and loan applications serving an average of 4.5 million customers a month. We built identity, authorization and audit trail systems and event-driven data platforms, and passed Visa, Mastercard, state and federal audits every year. I helped grow engineering from 2 people to 16 and wrote the hiring process. I led the move from on-prem to Azure and from waterfall to Scrum, with CI/CD, code scanning and edge protection along the way.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="mono teal small">n &lt; 3</p>
      <h3>Earlier</h3>
      <p>Internet Director at Equis International (Reuters), where I hired and led an early Agile/XP team on a $5M+ technical-analysis education and charting product. VP at ProTel Networks, a VoIP telecom startup acquired by Integra Telecom, running sales engineering, operations and hiring. Before and alongside that: HR SaaS at HRN, payment-processor web services at Galileo, and real-estate data warehousing at 360 House.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

